    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d102">

                <pb facs="0330" n="72" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg72"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/90</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-27T16:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 27, 1915, 4 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 8 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>464. Reported Germany will, on overrunning Servia, probably within few days, make
                    proposals peace, she demanding control Belgium, Poland, Servia, and have large
                    indemnity, while Bulgaria realizes aspirations Macedonia. Cardinal Hartmann’s
                    visit to Pope rumored to have reference to this.</p>
                <p>Italy is expected to send army to Albania, but report is she asks cooperation
                    other Allies.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
